2637	/// One review row against its own committed record (M17.5 F-27 / P1-A05, A06).
2638	///
2639	/// The previous version counted the record's `attempts` array and stopped, so a
2640	/// record of twelve EMPTY objects satisfied it, and a record whose own `result`
2641	/// was `fail` satisfied a packet row claiming `pass`. Everything a reviewer
2642	/// actually concluded was unread.
2643	#[allow(
2644	    clippy::too_many_lines,
2645	    reason = "one review record's contract is one contract; splitting it by line count would scatter the checks a reader must see together"
