2667	/// The record's digests: hex-shaped, and the raw one the SHA-256 of the
2668	/// retained answer (A09: a digest of nothing retained bound a record to no
2669	/// answer).
2670	/// A standing ruling on a class of reviewer finding (grilling decision 6,
2671	/// 2026-09-03): a finding Brian rules incorrect is cleared by a ruling
2672	/// commit signed against the pinned signer, never by editing the record.
2673	/// Rulings live in `docs/execution/rulings/*.md` with a front matter of
2674	/// `id`, `attack_class`, `target` (a repository path) and `status`
2675	/// (`draft` or `ruled`). A ruling cannot name its own commit, so the commit
2676	/// that counts is the last one that touched the ruling's file.
2677	#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Eq)]
2678	struct Ruling {
2679	    id: String,
2680	    attack_class: String,
2681	    target: String,
2682	    /// Phrases that must all appear in an attempt's prose for this ruling to
2683	    /// answer it. Blind pass 1 at aa00d41 (A08): matching on class and file
2684	    /// alone cleared an unrelated second claim in the same class and file —
2685	    /// R-001, written for "stage reads are leakage", silently cleared a
2686	    /// genuine untracked-chdir defect. A ruling answers a claim, not a
2687	    /// coordinate.
2688	    claim_requires: Vec<String>,
2689	    /// Phrases whose presence means this ruling does NOT answer the claim.
2690	    /// Blind pass 1 at 5fb1b57 (A08): a required phrase can be found inside a
2691	    /// sentence that negates it, so a ruling could suppress a defect it was
2692	    /// never shown. Required phrases say what a claim must be about;
2693	    /// excluded ones say what it must not be about.
2694	    claim_excludes: Vec<String>,
2695	    status: String,
2696	    file: String,
2697	}
