13183	/// Outcome of one generated case: the generator decides acceptance from the
13184	/// candidate itself, so `accepted`/`discards` are MEASURED, never assumed.
13185	enum Case {
13186	    /// In-domain and every metamorphic relation held. Carries a WITNESS of what
13187	    /// the code under test actually produced for this input.
13188	    ///
13189	    /// The witness exists because of M17.5 pass-2 #16. The evidence digest used
13190	    /// to absorb only the generator's RNG state, which made it a fingerprint of
13191	    /// the GENERATOR and provably independent of the code being tested: delete
13192	    /// every `ensure!` in every case function below and, so long as the number
13193	    /// of RNG draws is unchanged, the recorded `evidence_hash` is bit-identical.
13194	    /// Two different formatters would hash the same. A hash that cannot
13195	    /// distinguish the implementation from a no-op is not evidence about the
13196	    /// implementation.
13197	    ///
13198	    /// So each family now returns bytes derived from the output it observed, and
13199	    /// the runner folds those into the digest. An empty witness is refused.
13200	    Accepted {
13201	        category: &'static str,
13202	        witness: Vec<u8>,
13203	    },
13204	    /// Out of the declared domain; not evidence either way.
13205	    /// Out of domain, or a relation that legitimately does not apply. Carries
13206	    /// a WITNESS of WHY, for the same reason `Accepted` does (M17.5 F-30).
13207	    ///
13208	    /// The runner used to record a discard as the single byte `b"D"`, so the
13209	    /// digest absorbed the COUNT of discards and nothing about them. Six
13210	    /// mutants inside `case_repair`'s cycle construction survived on exactly
13211	    /// that: each kept the plan cyclic, so each still discarded, and the
13212	    /// evidence could not tell the shapes apart. ADR-0020 §4 says attempts and
13213	    /// discards are RECORDED; counting is not recording.
