 14225	/// Run the five families and return their evidence rows plus per-family
 14226	/// wall-clock timings.
 14227	///
 14228	/// The timings are returned SEPARATELY rather than embedded in the rows on
 14229	/// purpose: the rows are the hashable artifact and must be a pure function of
 14230	/// the seed and the code under test, while the timings are telemetry for the
 14231	/// operator (M17.5 pass-2 #18).
 14232	///
 14233	/// The case-count guard is a separate function so its BOUNDARIES are testable:
 14234	/// `>` -> `>=` at the safety limit can only be discriminated by a case that
 14235	/// runs at exactly 10,000,000, which no test can afford. Extracting the
 14236	/// predicate makes the boundary checkable in microseconds (M17.5 F-30).
 14237	/// Reject a case count that is zero or beyond the safety limit.
 14238	fn validate_case_count(cases: u64) -> Result<()> {
 14239	    if cases == 0 {
 14240	        anyhow::bail!("generated case count must be positive");
 14241	    }
 14242	    if cases > 10_000_000 {
 14243	        anyhow::bail!("generated case count exceeds safety limit: {cases} > 10000000");
 14244	    }
