 9832	/// Whether `anchor` could be the `before` text of `operator`'s prescribed
 9833	/// mutation. `verify_mutant_operator_patch` states the lexical contract over
 9834	/// both sides of a patch, but no patch exists at stage 1a, so that contract
 9835	/// had never been applied to an anchor: six mutants declared operators their
 9836	/// anchor could not support, including a `predicate-deletion` on a line with
 9837	/// no negation and a `missing-enum-dispatch` on a match ARM rather than the
 9838	/// match. This is the half of the contract the anchor alone can satisfy.
 9839	///
 9840	/// `<` and `>` are required to be spaced. Rustfmt writes comparisons that way
 9841	/// and generic parameters the other, and without the distinction every struct
 9842	/// field holding a `BTreeMap<K, V>` reads as a comparison.
 9843	/// Whether `trimmed` uses `||` as a disjunction rather than as a closure's
 9844	/// empty parameter list. Blind pass 1 at `ec045588` (A04): `ok_or_else(|| {`
 9845	/// carries a `||` that no short-circuit mutation can act on, and the
 9846	/// precondition counted it — the same mistake as a pattern's `|`, one token
 9847	/// wider. A disjunction has an operand to its left.
 9848	fn has_disjunction(trimmed: &str) -> bool {
 9849	    trimmed.match_indices("||").any(|(at, _)| {
 9850	        trimmed[..at]
 9851	            .trim_end()
 9852	            .chars()
 9853	            .next_back()
 9854	            .is_some_and(|previous| previous.is_alphanumeric() || matches!(previous, '_' | ')'))
 9855	    })
 9856	}
