 11437	/// picking a convenient definition, and ADR-0020 §3 forbids improvising
 11438	/// qualification semantics.
 11439	///
 11440	/// What is enforced instead is that the disclosure stays true. A prose scope
 11441	/// note rots the first time somebody adds a commit site — which is exactly the
 11442	/// defect A05 found in the original unscoped claim — so every durable
 11443	/// transition in tracked source must fall inside a declared in-scope subsystem
 11444	/// or a declared deferred surface, with counts matching exactly. A new
 11445	/// `txn.commit()` anywhere turns the packet red until it is either registered
